{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Delivered the RTL (axil_timer.v) and a self-checking testbench (axil_timer_tb.v) for the AXI4-Lite timer. Lint, simulation and synthesis are left to the platform. No formal_spec file is included, so the formal evidence requirements do not apply to this submission.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "Implementation decisions and spec interpretation", "summary": "The RTL follows the clocked-block order in [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1]: count step, then the expired clear and set, then the CTRL write, then the LOAD merge. This order produces the priorities in [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1] section 4. A count end beats a STATUS clear. A CTRL write beats the count end for EN and COUNT. A stop on a non-ending edge keeps the value that edge's decrement gives, and the testbench checks that interpretation. The held address, data and strobe registers are reset too, even though the microarchitecture says they need not be. This is a deliberate, harmless deviation that keeps every flop at a known value. The design serves [requirement:req-2b2b91a584]."}, {"kind": "open_item", "title": "Formal proof not submitted", "summary": "Section 8 of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1] and the verification plan in [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1] both ask for a SymbiYosys proof at ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8. This submission includes only a few design-intent assertions under `ifdef FORMAL` and no .sby file. The proof and its covers remain open work for a follow-up formal_spec submission."}], "files": [{"path": "axil_timer.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "axil_timer RTL", "summary": "This module implements the AXI4-Lite timer for [requirement:req-2b2b91a584]. It has the ports, register map, timer rules, SLVERR policy and synchronous reset of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1]. The structure follows [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1]: aw_held and w_held channel logic, arready = !rvalid, count_end = en && count <= 1, and irq = expired && ie. The address decode uses a generate block so that offsets from 0x10 up are unmapped when ADDR_WIDTH is above 4.", "entry": "axil_timer"}, {"path": "axil_timer_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "axil_timer self-checking testbench", "summary": "This is a directed, self-checking testbench for the coverage list in section 8 of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1]. It covers:\n- reset values and LOAD with partial or empty strobes\n- AW-first, W-first and simultaneous writes, with B and R back-pressure\n- a read and a write on the same edge\n- the COUNT read-only rule and unaligned addresses answering SLVERR\n- a CTRL write without wstrb[0]\n- one-shot counts of 5, 1 and 0 timed to the edge, with no second interrupt\n- IE set while an expiry is pending, and STATUS writes of 0 and without wstrb[0]\n- periodic counts over 4 periods, plus a clear on the count-end edge\n- a stop that freezes COUNT, a restart mid-count and on the end edge, and reset during a count\n- offsets from 0x10 up at ADDR_WIDTH 8\n\nAn ADDR_WIDTH 4 instance runs in lockstep with the ADDR_WIDTH 8 instance, matching the lanes in [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1]. Failures are reported with $error, and the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line is printed before $finish.", "entry": "axil_timer_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The testbench's expected cycle timings come from hand analysis of the RTL and the spec. They have not been confirmed by any simulation run.", "I expect the RTL to be clean under Verilator --lint-only -Wall and to synthesize without latches. Neither has been run."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Spec interpretation needing review: the spec says an EN-0 write keeps COUNT at its value. On an edge that is not a count end, the microarchitecture's ordering lets that edge's decrement happen first, then clears en. I implemented and test that behaviour, with frozen COUNT = LOAD - ((stop_edge - start_edge) mod LOAD) in periodic mode. If reviewers read the spec as 'no decrement on the stop edge', both the RTL and the testbench need to change. The testbench uses fork/join for the concurrent read and write, and # delays, so it needs Verilator --timing (implied by --binary) and Icarus with SystemVerilog system tasks enabled for $error. A formal_spec (.sby plus fuller properties at ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8) is still owed against spec section 8."}
